      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3147959662,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Is there some reason not to just assign the return status of `wtap_block_get_XXX_option_value()` to a `wtap_opttype_return_val` variable, and do `if (status == WTAP_OPTTYPE_SUCCESS) {` in the tests?\n\n(And are there warning options for any compilers that warn about converting integral types other than `bool`/`_Bool` to `bool`/`_Bool` without an explicit cast? I couldn't find any for GCC or Clang - `-Wint-in-bool-context` doesn't do the job, at least not for Apple clang version 15.0.0 (clang-1500.1.0.2.5) or gcc (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu-24.04.1) 13.3.0 - maybe newer versions warn about that.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
